<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nakhchivan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nakhichevan, Naxçıvan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nakhchivan is a city and region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">South Caucasus</a>, now an autonomous republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> separated from the rest of the country by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. The city was a residence of the Eldiguzid atabegs in the 12th century and later the seat of a khanate under Persian rule, annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1828. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it was contested by Armenia and Azerbaijan before becoming part of Soviet Azerbaijan.</p></div>
